			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add VS Code service decorator codegen pipeline and global bridge accessor\n\nAdd a new regex-based codegen system that walks the VS Code source tree and extracts `createDecorator(...)` sites along with their interface members:\n\n- `ExtractDecoratorMatch`: Captures decorator export names, tags, and JSDoc from `createDecorator<I<X>>('x')` patterns\n- `ExtractInterfaceMembers`: Extracts typed interface members (properties, methods, events, getters, setters) with parameters and doc comments\n- `IterateServiceDecorators`: Async iterator combining the walkers to yield one `ServiceDecoratorRecord` per decorator\n- `SourceTreeWalker`: Async-iterator over VS Code TypeScript sources, skipping test/build/node_modules directories\n- Typed records: `ServiceDecoratorRecord`, `InterfaceMemberRecord`, `CodegenProblem` ADT for error handling\n\nAlso adds `LandWorkbenchGlobal.ts` - a typed wrapper around `globalThis.__CEL_WIND__` that exposes `CELWind().RunPromise(...)` for Sky consumers without touching the raw global. Dispatches `cel:wind-ready` on installation.\n\nThis infrastructure enables automated Wind-side bridge shape generation from upstream VS Code source, with source-line back-links for traceability.",
			"SHA": "c4fc5b33d7395b7fd41a707edfbcc09b1bbc9eba"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:03:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1162,
				9
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add LandWorkbench composition layer and WorkbenchWorkspace service\n\nAdd a new LandWorkbench composition layer that merges all previously-added workbench-tier services (WorkbenchClipboard, Command, Dialog, Host, Keybinding, Lifecycle, Notification, Storage, Theme) plus the new WorkbenchWorkspace service into a single Layer for convenient consumption by Sky.\n\nAlso adds WorkbenchWorkspaceService - a new service bridging VS Code's native IWorkspaceService. Provides Snapshot (workspace id, folders, configuration), Folders (array of workspace folders), FolderForResource (lookup folder by URI), and OnFolderChange (stream of folder add/remove/change events). The Live implementation reads from globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Workspace and includes proper error handling via WorkbenchWorkspaceProblem ADT.\n\nThe LandWorkbenchLayer uses Layer.mergeAll so a failure in one service doesn't poison others, and LandWorkbenchRuntime provides a lazy singleton ManagedRuntime for efficient per-webview instantiation.",
			"SHA": "37f3cb97b14b50363c25099c04fb51abb6082b03"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:01:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1149,
				19
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add WorkbenchClipboard, WorkbenchHost, and WorkbenchKeybinding services\n\nAdd three new workbench-tier Effect-TS service layers that bridge VS Code's native workbench services:\n\n- WorkbenchClipboardService: Read/write text and resources via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Clipboard. Provides ReadText, WriteText, ReadResources, WriteResources with typed Problem ADT for bridge unavailability and operation failures.\n\n- WorkbenchHostService: Host operations (reload, restart, close, focus, open window) via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Host. Includes OnDidChangeFocus stream for focus state changes.\n\n- WorkbenchKeybindingService: Keybinding lookup and resolution via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Keybinding. Exposes Lookup, Resolve, and Chords stream for keybinding dispatch events.\n\nEach service follows the established Wind pattern with Context.Tag, interface, Live implementation (runtime bridge), and Problem ADT for error cases. Also adds WorkbenchWorkspaceProblem type.",
			"SHA": "b91de584652edf03f663b8b77d03e3d2670868a9"
		},
